<!--Post: 3419--><!--Time: 1104885089-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3419"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Curious2<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Curious2<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 4:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have read on several forums that it is <BR>possible that BTK is from a prominent family? <BR>Where is this information from?  Anyone know?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3419-->
<!--Post: 3421--><!--Time: 1104886056-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3421"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 4:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here is the storie: <BR> <BR><a href="http://groups.google.dk/groups?q=%22%2Bstable%22%2B%2B%2Bbtk&amp;hl=en&amp;lr=&amp;selm=stu9c.14941%24mf.3572%40okepread05&amp;rnum=1" target=_top>http://groups.google.dk/groups?q=%22&#43;stable%22&#43;&#43;%2 Bbtk&amp;hl=en&amp;lr=&amp;selm=stu9c.14941%24mf.3572%40okepre ad05&amp;rnum=1</a> <BR> <BR>I heard over and over was that the BTK was the member of the <BR>&#62; family who owned Bridle and Saddle, and that he was never arrested <BR>&#62; because of the family&#39;s money and influence. <BR> <BR>skov <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3421-->
<!--Post: 3430--><!--Time: 1104891627-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3430"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 6:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think that &#34;from a prominent family&#34; stuff springs up in a lot of unsolved murders, like an urban legend. <BR> <BR>The town my husband&#39;s from had an unsolved murder.  It got a lot of headlines and eventually the rumor was that the killer was from a local prominent family, etc. <BR> <BR>There are several cases in the town I&#39;m from that are the same way.  I think it&#39;s an attempt to explain why no one&#39;s been arrested and charged.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3430-->
<!--Post: 3432--><!--Time: 1104891851-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3432"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 6:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Does anyone have any particulars as to this family&#39;s money and influence? Owning a Bridle and Saddle doesn&#39;t quite cut the mustard with me. In what way are they influential? Seems like I have never heard anything about them other than their connection to the Bridle and Saddle. Now, I did stumble across something that I found to be quite interesting last summer. While researching former Police Captain Bobby Stout I found a geneology page with familial ties &#40; name-wise &#41; to the surnames Bruce, Killman, Anna and William Thomas. Let me see if I can find the link.  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3432-->
<!--Post: 3433--><!--Time: 1104891959-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3433"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 6:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here it is: <BR><a href="http://members.aol.com/ftnkid/" target=_top>http://members.aol.com/ftnkid/</a> <BR> <BR>What do you think?  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3433-->
<!--Post: 3457--><!--Time: 1104939046-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3457"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Catcher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Catcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 7:30 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nice find!  Hmmmmmmm...my girlfriend&#39;s family is/was all WPD officer&#39;s.  Maybe I can query them on your findings!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3457-->
<!--Post: 3470--><!--Time: 1104947526-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3470"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 9:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Check out the names at the bottom of this page: <BR> <BR><a href="http://members.aol.com/thetoofish/genealogy/lines/index/ind0002.html#I86" target=_top>http://members.aol.com/thetoofish/genealogy/lines/ index/ind0002.html#I86</a> <BR> <BR>And here: <BR><a href="http://members.aol.com/thetoofish/genealogy/lines/index/ind0004.html#I14" target=_top>http://members.aol.com/thetoofish/genealogy/lines/ index/ind0004.html#I14</a> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3470-->
<!--Post: 3493--><!--Time: 1104965015-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3493"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 2:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Cougar, <BR> One of the posts about a S&amp;M group had a link to posts on a Bondage&#40;?&#41; Message Board by a guy calling himself &#34;BTK&#34; and he had/has a signature poem &#40;I think it is a poem&#41; about being &#34;Billy The Kid&#34; from Wheeling West Virgina. This would explain the &#34;K&#34; but it seems likely a sinister and thinnly veiled ref to &#34;the&#34; BTK we seek here. <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t know exactly where it is and i don&#39;t want to see that sick crap again but interesting that your link has &#34;William Kidd &amp; Killman&#34; both as relatives. <BR> <BR>Prominent Families... I don&#39;t know. <BR> <BR>I do know that BTKs accent as heard on his infamous phone call sounds like a Pittsburgh Accent to me and Wheeling is just down the road. <BR> <BR>Also.. there is a Pittsburgh connect with someone I think is person of interest... a relative of a possible victim. Tom decoded to delete all refs to this person but there are some very odd connections and this person &#34;is&#34; prominent by the nature of his position in the Wichita Area Community.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3493-->
<!--Post: 3494--><!--Time: 1104965509-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3494"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 2:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If nobody knows BTK&#39;s identity, how would they be able to determine the financial status of his family?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3494-->
<!--Post: 3504--><!--Time: 1104970588-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3504"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 4:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Good question, Tom. I guess maybe people are referring to their suspect - one whom they believe to BTK.  <BR> <BR>Check these names out on the same site that I referenced above: <BR> <BR><a href="http://members.aol.com/thetoofish/genealogy/lines/d0000/g0000042.html#I14" target=_top>http://members.aol.com/thetoofish/genealogy/lines/ d0000/g0000042.html#I14</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3504-->
<!--Post: 3589--><!--Time: 1105048438-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3589"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ksgirl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ksgirl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 1:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Has anyone looked for info on Bridle &amp; Saddle Stables?  I tried to find info on Access Kansas but couldn&#39;t.  Any ideas?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3589-->
<!--Post: 3811--><!--Time: 1105257015-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3811"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->J_eric<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->J_eric<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 08, 2005 - 11:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The &#34;influential family&#34; concept goes all the way back to Jack The Ripper, who was supposed to be a member of the royal family.  In reality, most serial killers turn out to be no-accounts, drifters and, if permanent residents, rather unimportant folk around town.  &#40;Gacy was a contractor but not a particularly successful one as I recall.&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3811-->
<!--Post: 3818--><!--Time: 1105295065-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3818"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 09, 2005 - 10:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Right as usual J Eric.  But I would add that the &#34;influential family&#34; goes back in either fact or legend.  Robin Hood is the farthest back I can think of, and while a modern day hero he was an outlaw. <BR>Unless GOOD evidence surfaces this will remain an urban legeng.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3818-->
